        "title": "2015 X4 N20 Lower-Engine Whine Requires Timing-Chain Diagnosis",
        "description": "BMW SIB 11 03 17 identifies F26 X4 xDrive28i N20 vehicles produced from March 2014 through February 2015. A lower-engine whine that increases with engine speed can be associated with timing-chain or oil-pump-drive-chain wear; the bulletin does not declare every X4 or every N20 defective.",
        "solution": "Confirm the exact xDrive28i variant, N20 engine, production date and VIN eligibility, then have a BMW-qualified technician reproduce the noise and follow current BMW diagnosis before replacing anything. The historical seven-year/70,000-mile coverage was a limited warranty extension, not a recall, and is not a current coverage promise. ShowMeTheParts established category-level fitment only, so no commerce link is approved.",
